            <ArticleTitle>Acute abdomen due to Brucella melitensis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>204-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A case of acute abdomen caused by a Brucella melitensis is reported. The patient presented with biliary involvement in the form of acute acalculous cholecystitis and developed acute appendicitis that resulted in his surgical treatment.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
